# Build-time, and PUBLIC BY DESIGN.
#
# Vite reads this file during `npm run build`, so these are compiled into the
# bundle. That is not a leak: both values are public the moment the page is
# served, and both are protected by restriction rather than by secrecy.
#
#   VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_EMBED_KEY  sits in the map iframe URL. Protect it by
#                               restricting the key to the Maps Embed API and
#                               by HTTP referrer to the site's domain.
#   VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY     Cloudflare publish this one deliberately. The
#                               secret half is what actually verifies, and it
#                               lives server-side.
#
# They are committed rather than set in the Cloudflare dashboard because build
# variables and runtime bindings are configured in different places, which is
# an easy thing to get wrong: a build variable set as a runtime binding is
# simply absent when Vite runs, and the map silently falls back with no error.
# Committing them makes the build reproducible and removes two things from the
# dashboard.
#
# NEVER put a server-side key here. GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY, BREVO_API_KEY and
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY belong in the dashboard and nowhere else.

VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_EMBED_KEY=
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAEdJybgPsOXjaVlW
